# One account. App-leg phones register over TLS to the light server with
# SIP Digest using their enrolled device's id and token as AUTH_USER /
# AUTH_PASS (the server refuses a registration without them, or for a user
# the device is not enrolled for). A desk phone registers over UDP to the
# harness PBX with the PBX's Digest credentials and G.711 only, like a real
# desk phone.
# @REGINT@ is the registration interval; 0 = start unregistered (the wake test
# registers on demand via ctrl_tcp, as the woken app would).
# @OUTBOUND@ (optional) is an outbound proxy by address, like a real phone
# uses; libre resolves the AOR domain by DNS only (never /etc/hosts).
# @MEDIAENC@ is ";mediaenc=srtp-mand" on the app leg (TLS to the light
# server: SRTP is mandatory there, SPEC §4.4 rule 4) and empty for the desk
# phone (plain RTP to the PBX, like the trunk).
# @ANSWERMODE@ is auto (the default: every call is answered at once, so the
# tests can assert on audio) or manual (the phone rings and never answers —
# for tests about what happens while a callee is still ringing).
<sip:@SIP_USER@@@SIP_DOMAIN@;transport=@TRANSPORT@>;auth_user=@AUTH_USER@;auth_pass=@AUTH_PASS@;regint=@REGINT@;answermode=@ANSWERMODE@@MEDIAENC@;audio_codecs=@CODECS@@OUTBOUND@
